# Weapons

> **Source of truth для weapon customization, composition, і content:** `docs/ai/weapon-builder/README.md`. This file describes runtime behaviour (FSM, aiming, ADS, visualization) shared by all assembled weapons.

## Quick reference

Player weapons are **assembled from Weapon Builder**. Composition lives in `ItemState.WeaponConfiguration`; runtime state in `WeaponEntityState` with cached `Stats` block.

Key files:
- `State/WeaponEntityState.cs` — composition refs (PayloadCore, DeliveryCore, ExoticMod?), cached `WeaponStats`, runtime phase fields, `WeaponPrefab` + `PayloadPrefab` GameObject refs (Tier 8)
- `State/PayloadCoreDefinition.cs` + subclasses (Ballistic / Laser / Rocket / Foam) — SO-driven stats per rarity tier; `AttachmentPrefab` field
- `State/DeliveryCoreDefinition.cs` — SO-driven stats + `FiringPattern` enum; `WeaponPrefab` field
- `Systems/WeaponSyncSystem.cs` — assembly pipeline (config → runtime state) + visualization prefab resolution
- `Systems/WeaponAssemblySystem.cs` — `TryAssemble(config) → result`; ghost-weapon path on failure (D7)
- `Systems/WeaponStatComposer.cs` — pure: (Payload + Delivery + Rarity) → WeaponStats
- `Systems/ShootingSystem.cs` — dispatch по `FiringPattern`, charge gate для Laser
- `Systems/WeaponStateMachineSystem.cs` — FSM phases
- `View/WeaponView.cs` — visualization: PayloadMount socket, AttachPayload, procedural recoil kick on Fire
- `View/CharacterBody.cs` — `SwapWeaponModel(prefab, idForTracking, payloadPrefab)` instantiates delivery + attaches payload at socket

Stats live in SO assets at `Assets/Resources/WeaponBuilder/*` (Payloads/, Deliveries/, CoreDefinitionDatabase). No hardcoded tables — values edited in Inspector.

## Weapon State Machine

`WeaponPhase` enum on `WeaponEntityState`:

| Phase | Trigger → next | Notes |
|-------|---------------|-------|
| `Ready` | AttackPressed → `Charging` (Laser payload) or `Firing`; ReloadPressed → `Reloading` | Idle, accepts input |
| `Charging` | AttackJustReleased → `Firing` / `Bursting` with charge-scaled stats; PendingSwap → `Unequipping` | Tier 2 + Tau-cannon mechanic (2026-05-06): hold-to-charge, fire-on-release |
| `Firing` | Next tick → `Cooldown` | 1-tick marker; ShootingSystem spawned projectiles |
| `Bursting` | LaserBurstInterval-paced auto-fire; BurstShotsRemaining=0 → `Cooldown`; PendingSwap → `Unequipping` | 2026-05-06 — laser+Auto delivery після release fires 1..6 shots scaled з chargeRatio |
| `Cooldown` | FireInterval elapsed → `Ready` | Inter-shot gap |
| `Equipping` / `Unequipping` | EquipTime/UnequipTime elapsed → `Ready` / swap | Weapon draw/holster |
| `Reloading` | ReloadTime elapsed → `Ready` + fill mag | `AmmoSystem.CompleteReload` |

**Laser charge-up mechanic** (2026-05-06, HL Tau cannon style):
- AttackPressed on laser → `Charging`, ChargeStartTime = elapsed
- Holding past ChargeTime keeps weapon in Charging at chargeRatio = 1.0 (no auto-fire — must release)
- AttackJustReleased → fires charged shot at clamp((elapsed - chargeStart) / chargeTime, 0, 1)
- Damage scaling: damage *= lerp(0.3, 1.0, chargeRatio)
- VFX scaling: BeamFlashPresenter reads chargeRatio from ProjectileSpawned.CurrentHp

**Laser rifle burst** (laser + Auto delivery only):
- After release-fire, burstCount = round(lerp(1, 6, chargeRatio))
- If burstCount > 1 → enter Bursting phase, ShootingSystem.TickBurst auto-fires every LaserBurstInterval = 0.07s
- Each burst shot uses cached BurstChargeRatio, recomputes muzzle/aim (tracks rotation)
- Out of ammo mid-burst → terminates early → Cooldown
- Other laser deliveries (SingleAction/Scatter) → single charged shot, no burst

Tick order: `Movement → WeaponEquip → WeaponStateMachine → Aiming → Shooting → ...`

Events: `WeaponFired`, `WeaponEquipStarted/Finished`, `WeaponUnequipStarted`, `WeaponReloadStarted/Finished`, `WeaponDryFired`, `WeaponChargeStarted/Completed/Cancelled`, `WeaponAssemblyFailed`.

Bots do NOT use this FSM — they remain on `LastFireTime` cooldown in `BotCombatSystem`.

### Trigger semantics — semi-auto vs full-auto (2026-05-10)

Player input is gated per `FiringPattern` after the pattern dispatch in `ShootingSystem.Tick`:

| Pattern | Trigger | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `Auto` (Rifle) | `AttackPressed` (held) | Full-auto — fires every `FireInterval` while LMB held |
| `Single` (Pistol) | `AttackJustPressed` (rising edge) | One click = one shot. Holding LMB through Cooldown does NOT re-fire — must release + press |
| `Scatter` (Shotgun) | `AttackJustPressed` (rising edge) | Same as Single — single blast per click |
| Any + Laser payload | `AttackJustReleased` (release) | Charge-release path; semi-auto gate bypassed via `releaseFire` flag |

Implementation: `IInputAdapter.AttackJustPressed` (rising-edge, `WasPressedThisFrame()`). In `ShootingSystem`:

```csharp
bool semiAuto = pattern == FiringPattern.Single || pattern == FiringPattern.Scatter;
if (semiAuto && !releaseFire && !input.AttackJustPressed) return;
```

Bots run the legacy `LastFireTime` cooldown path — not affected.

## Ammo & Reload

Magazine ammo + reserve ammo (from player inventory backpack).

- `weapon.AmmoType` — identifier from payload (e.g. `"Ammo_Rifle"`, `"Ammo_EnergyCell"`); null for bots
- `weapon.Stats.MagazineSize`, `weapon.AmmoInMagazine` — max / current
- `weapon.Stats.ReloadTime` — reload duration

`AmmoSystem` (stateless static): `CountReserve`, `ConsumeAmmo`, `CompleteReload`, `CanReload`.

1 trigger pull = 1 ammo (Scatter spawns N pellets but consumes 1).

Ammo types defined in `ItemDefinition.BuildRegistry()`. Penetration/ArmorDamage/BleedChance modifiers stored on the ammo `ItemDefinition` and added to weapon base stats **in ShootingSystem on fire** (separate channel from cached `Stats`).

## Projectile Stat Composition

```
totalPenetration = weapon.Stats.BasePenetration + ammoDef.Penetration
totalArmorDamage = weapon.Stats.BaseArmorDamage + ammoDef.ArmorDamage
totalBleedChance = weapon.Stats.BaseBleedChance + ammoDef.BleedChance
```

Damage and projectile speed scaled additionally by `ShootingConfig.DamageMultiplier` / `ProjectileSpeedMultiplier` (DevCheats). Result lands in `ProjectileEntityState` + emits `ProjectileSpawned`.

## Projectile Collision (hit detection)

`View/ProjectileView.SyncFromState` resolves hits per-frame in two stages:

1. **Start-overlap probe** (2026-05-09) — `Physics.OverlapSphereNonAlloc(oldPos, hitRadius)`. Unity's `SphereCast` returns no hit when the sphere already overlaps a collider at the start. At point-blank distances `CharacterBody.LateUpdate` weapon pullback (see below) retracts the muzzle **inside** the target capsule — without the probe the bullet would silently fly through. Probe registers the damageable immediately, hit point = `oldPos`, normal = `-direction`.
2. **SphereCast** along movement path (`oldPos → newPos`, `DefaultRaycastLayers`, `Collide`). Existing flight path.

On hit: `IDamageableView` lookup → `RaidSession.ReportHit(HitSignal)` for characters, `ReportCollision(CollisionSignal)` for walls.

## Weapon Barrel Pullback (2026-05-09)

When the player's barrel pokes into a wall or another character, the WeaponPivot retracts smoothly along `-forward` so the muzzle (and projectile spawn) stays clear. Without this, bullets would spawn behind cover or past an enemy at point-blank.

`View/CharacterBody.LateUpdate` (execution order 2000, after presenters rotate the pivot):
- **Cast:** `Physics.SphereCastNonAlloc` from body-XZ at `ProjectileSpawnHeight` toward `MuzzlePoint`, distance = body→muzzle + `WeaponLength`
- **Mask:** `BotConstants.VisionBlockingMask | (1 << LayerUtils.Player) | (1 << LayerUtils.Bot)` — walls + live character shells. Ragdoll layer (9) excluded → corpses don't twitch the barrel
- **Filter:** skip self root + skip any root with `RagdollController`
- **Retract:** `WeaponPullbackMath.ComputeRetract` (pure math, fully unit-tested) = `1 - distFromPivot/weaponLength`, clamped 0..1
- **Apply:** lerps pivot.localPosition toward `rest + back × Amount × retract`. Muzzle is a grandchild → retracts automatically

Combined with the ProjectileView overlap probe: point-blank into a character spawns the bullet inside the enemy capsule, probe registers the hit on first sync → reliable point-blank kills.

DevCheats (`Weapon` section): `WeaponPullbackEnabled`, `WeaponLength`, `WeaponPullbackAmount`, `WeaponPullbackSpeed`, `WeaponPullbackRadius`, `BotPullbackCheckRateHz` (12 Hz for bots), `BotPullbackLodDistance`.

## Convergence & Parallax Correction

Projectile direction blends two sources in `ShootingSystem`:
1. **Parallax-corrected** — adjusts for camera height so trail passes through crosshair
2. **Convergence** — toward `input.ConvergencePoint` (3D collider raycast hit)
3. **Blend** — `Lerp(parallax, convergence, ConvergenceBlend)`

**AimUp:** when convergence hits a character, projectile angles slightly up (`AimUpHeightRatio`) to intersect upper body — enables headshot detection from top-down camera.

**Lock-on override (2026-05-10):** when `convergence` hits a damageable (`IDamageableView` in hierarchy of hit collider), `blend` is forced to `1.0` — full convergence, 3D-accurate direction. Without override, at top-down + side-angle configurations the mid-blend (~0.3) would land trajectory past the capsule edge. Non-damageable cases (ground, walls, empty space) keep the user-tuned `ConvergenceBlend` so visual "trail through cursor" feel is preserved.

Spawn Y forced to `cfg.ProjectileSpawnHeight` to reduce parallax.

DevCheats (ShootingConfig): `ParallaxCorrection`, `ConvergenceBlend`, `ConvergenceAimUp`, `AimUpHeightRatio`, `ProjectileSpawnHeight`.

## ADS (Aim Down Sights)

Continuous blend `player.AdsBlend` (0=hip, 1=ADS), lerped each tick by `input.AdsPressed` and `AdsTransitionTime`.

Aiming: `AimFollowSharpness *= Lerp(1, AdsAimFollowMultiplier, AdsBlend)`; recoil decay `*= Lerp(1, AdsRecoilRecoveryMultiplier, AdsBlend)`.
Shooting: recoil kick `*= Lerp(1, AdsRecoilMultiplier, AdsBlend)` (default 0.6x).
Movement: speed `*= Lerp(1, AdsMoveSpeedMultiplier, AdsBlend)` (default 0.7x).
Crosshair (`AimCursorOverlay`): gap/bloom lerp toward ADS values; top crosshair line fades out.

DevCheats (ADS section): `AdsTransitionTime`, `AdsMoveSpeedMultiplier`, `AdsAimFollowMultiplier`, `AdsRecoilMultiplier`, `AdsRecoilRecoveryMultiplier`, `AdsBaseGap`, `AdsBloomExtraGap`.

## Dual-Layer Aiming

Player aiming has two layers:
1. **RawAimPoint** — instant world position from mouse (player intent)
2. **WeaponAimPoint** — smoothed toward Raw + recoil offset

Key fields:
- `PlayerEntityState`: `RawAimPoint`, `WeaponAimPoint`, `AimDirection`, `FacingDirection`, `IsADS`, `AdsBlend`
- `WeaponEntityState.Stats`: `AimFollowSharpness`, `RecoilKickForward`, `RecoilKickSide`, `RecoilRecoverySpeed`
- `WeaponEntityState` runtime: `RecoilOffset`

Smoothing: position-based exponential `Lerp(current, target, 1 - exp(-sharpness * dt))`. Recoil: subtract-apply pattern in AimingSystem separates tracking (AimFollowSharpness) from decay (RecoilRecoverySpeed).

DevCheats: `AimSplitEnabled` (false = instant follow), `AimFollowMultiplier`, `RecoilMultiplier`, `RecoilForwardMultiplier`, `RecoilSideMultiplier`, `RecoilRecoveryMultiplier`.

## 3D Modular Visualization

Tier 8 (2026-04-30): each weapon = runtime composition of two visual modules.

**Pipeline:**
```
WeaponConfiguration → WeaponSyncSystem.BuildWeaponForItem
  resolves DeliveryDefinition.WeaponPrefab + PayloadDefinition.AttachmentPrefab
WeaponEntityState { WeaponPrefab, PayloadPrefab }
  PlayerView.SyncFromState
CharacterBody.SwapWeaponModel(prefab, id, payloadPrefab)
  Instantiate(delivery prefab) under WeaponPivot
  WeaponView.AttachPayload(payloadPrefab) child of PayloadMount socket
```

**Symmetric composition:**
- **Delivery prefab** carries body silhouette + Animator + sockets (`DeliveryBody` mesh, `MuzzlePoint`, `RightHandGrip`, `PayloadMount`) + WeaponView component
- **Payload prefab** wraps barrel/emitter mesh; spawned under PayloadMount on equip

PolygonApocalypse modular parts (`SM_Wep_Mod_Body_*`, `SM_Wep_Mod_Barrel_*`) used for current 6 archetypes (Pistol/Rifle/Shotgun × Ballistic/Laser).

**Procedural recoil** (`WeaponView.TriggerRecoilKick`): on `PlayFire(duration)` body kicks back -Z on `_recoilKickDistance` (default 0.04m), eases out-quad to rest over `max(0.06, duration*0.4)`. Per-prefab `[SerializeField]`. Replaces Mecanim animation paths stale after symmetric pivot.

**Optional payload Animator** — payload prefab may carry own Animator (e.g. Laser pulse) without interference. Real animation polish — Tier 9.

**Adding new content (Tier 3+):**
- Create `<Name>.asset` SO + add to `CoreDefinitionDatabase`
- Run `Tools → Weapon Builder → Create Module Prefabs` → primitive prefab + wired refs (idempotent)
- Replace primitive content artist drop-in (no code/SO touch)
- Detailed workflow: `docs/ai/weapon-builder/README.md` (Workflow section)

